Article 2 (Definitions) The terms used in these Rules are defined as follows: <Amended on November 9, 2021; October 1, 2025>
1. "Mining and Manufacturing Survey" means a survey conducted by the Government at a specific point in time to identify the industrial structure, management status, etc. of establishments operating industries under the subparagraphs of Article 3 within the territory of the Republic of Korea;
2. "Establishment" means an enterprise or part thereof that independently conducts a single or principal economic activity at a fixed place;
3. "Survey conducting agency" means a person that performs survey affairs under delegated authority of the Administrator of the National Data Agency concerning the Mining and Manufacturing Survey pursuant to Article 15;
4. "Survey personnel" means any of the following persons:
  (a) Enumerators who prepare survey forms and collect data for the Mining and Manufacturing Survey;
  (b) Survey supervisors who guide and support enumerators;
  (c) Other personnel who support survey affairs and review and supplement completed survey forms.
